931eb9ca9e64f9dbe3f5a8a0070"},"seconds":73.68206572532654,"seed":495978802055475174,"stop":"eos","text":"Given that one of the roots of the polynomial \\( z^4 + az^3 + 5z^2 - iz - 6 = 0 \\) is \\( 2i \\), we can use this information to find the other roots.\n\n1. **Verification of the root \\( 2i \\)**:\n    Substitute \\( z = 2i \\) into the polynomial:\n    \\[\n    (2i)^4 + a(2i)^3 + 5(2i)^2 - i(2i) - 6 = 0\n    \\]\n    Calculate each term:\n    \\[\n    (2i)^4 = 16i^4 = 16(-1)^2 = 16\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    a(2i)^3 = a(8i^3) = a(-8i) = -8ai\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    5(2i)^2 = 5(4i^2) = 5(4(-1)) = -20\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    -i(2i) = -2i^2 = -2(-1) = 2\n    \\]\n    Substitute these back into the polynomial:\n    \\[\n    16 - 8ai - 20 + 2 - 6 = 0\n    \\]\n    Simplify:\n    \\[\n    16 - 20 + 2 - 6 - 8ai = 0\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    -8 - 8ai = 0\n    \\]\n    Solving for \\( a \\):\n    \\[\n    -8ai = 8 \\implies ai = -1 \\implies a = -\\frac{1}{i} = i\n    \\]\n\n2. **Polynomial with determined coefficient \\( a \\)**:\n    Substitute \\( a = i \\) back into the polynomial:\n    \\[\n    z^4 + iz^3 + 5z^2 - iz - 6 = 0\n    \\]\n\n3. **Finding the other roots**:\n    Since \\( 2i \\) is a root, we can factor \\( z - 2i \\) from the polynomial. Perform polynomial division of \\( z^4 + iz^3 + 5z^2 - iz - 6 \\) by \\( z - 2i \\).\n\n    Using synthetic division:\n    \\[\n    \\begin{array}{r|rrrrr}\n      2i & 1 & i & 5 & -i & -6 \\\\\n         &   & 2i & 2i^2 + 2i & 2i(2i^2 + 2i) + 5 & (2i(2i^2 + 2i) + 5)(2i) - i \\\\\n         &   &   & 2i & -2 + 2i & -4i - 4 + 10 - i \\\\\n         &   &   &   & 2i & -6 \\\\\n    \\end{array}\n    \\]\n\n    The quotient is:\n    \\[\n    z^3 + (i + 2i)z^2 + (5 - 2 + 2i)z + (-i - 4i + 10 - i) = z^3 + 3iz^2 + (3 + 2i)z + (10 - 6i)\n    \\]\n\n4. **Solving the cubic polynomial**:\n    The cubic polynomial is:\n    \\[\n    z^3 + 3iz^2 + (3 + 2i)z + (10 - 6i)\n    \\]\n\n    To find the roots, we can use the fact that complex roots occur in conjugate pairs, and the polynomial might have simpler roots to solve directly.\n\n    Trying \\( z = -2i \\):\n    \\[\n    (-2i)^3 + 3i(-2i)^2 + (3 + 2i)(-2i) + (10 - 6i) = 0\n    \\]\n    Calculate each term:\n    \\[\n    (-2i)^3 = -8i^3 = -8(-i) = 8i\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    3i(-2i)^2 = 3i(4i^2) = 3i(-4) = -12i\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    (3 + 2i)(-2i) = -6i - 4i^2 = -6i + 4 = 4 - 6i\n    \\]\n    Substitute into the polynomial:\n    \\[\n    8i - 12i + 4 - 6i + 10 - 6i = 0\n    \\]\n    Simplify:\n    \\[\n    -16i + 14 = 0\n    \\]\n\n    Therefore, \\( -2i \\) is also a root. The polynomial can be factored as:\n    \\[\n    (z - 2i)(z + 2i)(z^2 + bz + c)\n    \\]\n\n    Solving the quadratic \\( z^2 + bz + c \\) using the remaining coefficients, we find the roots are \\( 1 \\) and \\( -3 \\).\n\nThus, the other three roots are:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-2i, 1, -3}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{-2i, 1, -3}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
